\ A quotation literal reading a local, handed to a word rather than inlined, in a binary with no
\ interpreter. Its compiled body runs in place of the captured closure and resolves `label`
\ without the captured scope, so it would reach the module word. The build refuses the word
\ rather than print the wrong label.

label: ( -- s ) [ "MODULE" ] ;
runner: ( q -- s ) [ call ] ;

reified: ( -- s ) [
  label: "OWN" ;
  label drop
  [ label ] runner
] ;

reified print-line
